<%# Shared chrome for every Devise screen, so sign in, sign up, password reset,
    confirmation and unlock are one shape rather than five near-misses.

    `links: false` for a screen that is not a Devise one. The link row below calls
    `resource_name` and `devise_mapping`, which only exist inside a Devise
    controller — so the two-factor challenge, which looks like a sign-in screen
    and is served by a controller of our own, raises a NameError without it. The
    challenge carries its own actions ("send a new code", "not you?") and would
    have nothing to say in that row anyway. %>
<% show_links = local_assigns.fetch(:links, true) %>

<%# EVERY AUTH SCREEN IS A REAL PAGE LOAD, and that is here for password
    managers rather than for anything a person sees.

    A manager finds the fields to offer by scanning the document when one loads.
    Turbo Drive does not load documents — it fetches the response and swaps the
    <body> — so arriving at the sign-in form from anywhere inside the
    application produced no new document and no scan, and the form was never
    offered a saved password. Measured over CDP: clicking "Forgot your password?"
    and then "Sign in" fired two `Page.navigatedWithinDocument` events and zero
    `Page.frameNavigated`.

    `turbo-visit-control: reload` makes Turbo hand the visit back to the browser
    instead of rendering it, so these screens always arrive as documents. The
    cost is one full load on a page somebody sees once a month; the alternative
    is a login form that types itself only if you got to it by pasting the URL.

    The other half of the same problem is on the forms themselves — a Turbo
    SUBMISSION is a fetch too, and a manager that never sees a navigation after a
    password goes out never offers to save it. See the `turbo: false` on each
    credential form, and spec/requests/password_manager_spec.rb, which pins both
    halves. -%>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-visit-control" content="reload">
<% end %>

<div class="shell max-w-md py-16">
  <div class="pt-5 rule-heavy">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-5"><%= title %></h1>
    <% if local_assigns[:subtitle].present? %>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-2"><%= subtitle %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8"><%= yield %></div>

  <% if show_links %>
    <div class="mt-8 rule pt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-[13px] text-ink-2">
      <%= render "devise/shared/links" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
